WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.200
A craftsperson can begin
assembly by creating the

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.270
valve that covers the
intake hole.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.140
She installs a rounded
length of wire, stapling

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.930
it in such a way as to
create enough tension for

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:15.040
the wire to act as a
spring.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.850
This step completes the
interior of the bellows.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.910
She starts by wrapping a
pre-cut piece of locally

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.030
sourced sheep's leather
around one handle and

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.790
attaching the leather in
place with small nails,

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.410
carefully hammering a
series of closely spaced

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.630
upholstery tacks at
regular intervals.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:41.100
The artisan can now
attach the second half by

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.290
repeating the operation
on the other side of the

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:47.530
leather. The artisan
uses a section of pre-cut

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.930
leather to form the
hinge necessary for the

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:51.880
proper functioning of
the bellows.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:55.000
The size, position and
tack pattern must all be

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.970
precise in order for the
tool to open and close

00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:59.680
smoothly and easily.

